===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[treat]] as a [[single]] [[unit]]; to [[group]] [[together]] in a [[casual]] or [[chaotic]] manner (as if forming an [[ill-defined]] [[#Noun|lump]] of the items).
#: {{ux|en|People tend to '''lump''' turtles and tortoises together, when in fact they are different creatures.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Daniel Taylor|title=Luis Suárez strikes twice as Barcelona teach Manchester City a lesson|work={{w|The Guardian}} (London)|date=24 February 2015|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/feb/24/manchester-city-barcelona-champions-league-match-report
|passage=Pellegrini’s decision to operate with both Edin Dzeko and Agüero in attack certainly looks misjudged bearing in mind that the first way to stop Barcelona is usually to try to crowd midfield and restrict space. Yet it would be wrong to '''lump''' all the blame on the manager’s tactics.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[bear]] (a [[heavy]] or [[awkward]] [[burden]]); to [[carry]] (something [[unwieldy]]) from one place to another.
#* '''1876''', ''Belgravia'' (volume 30, page 131)
#*: Well, a male body was brought to a certain surgeon by a man he had often employed, and the pair '''lumped''' it down on the dissecting table, and then the vendor received his money and went.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=World's End for Sir Oswald: Portraits of Working-class Life in Pre-war London|author=Alf Goldberg|year=1999|publisher=Book Guild|isbn=978-1-85776-485-7|passage=I never ceased to be amazed at his prowess at being able to '''lump''' two-hundredweight sacks of coal, which seemed as big as he was, up perhaps four flights of narrow stairs}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[burden]] (someone) with an [[undesired]] [[task]] or [[responsibility]].
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=The Channel Dash / Operation Cerberus - How to win through refuge in audacity|date=9 January 2019|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QNE0CkSsfJc|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220724023416/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QNE0CkSsfJc|archivedate=24 July 2022|accessdate=18 December 2022|time=15:17|text=The ''Luftwaffe'', at this point, was still refusing to play ball completely, however.  But someone decided to '''lump''' Adolf Galland with command of the air operation, and he decided to work with ''Luftflotte'' 3, mobilizing their training units to make up the numbers, since large numbers of that particular formation's fighters had been diverted to the campaign in Russia, which was why the fighter numbers were so much lower than they had been the previous year.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[hit]] or [[strike]] (a person).
#* '''1962''', Floyd Patterson, ''Victory Over Myself'' (page 63)
#*: If that's the only way you can fight, then you'd better be prepared to get '''lumped'''.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[form]] a [[#Noun|lump]] or lumps.
#* '''2004''', ''Creative Gifts: Quick & Easy Projects'' (page 44)
#*: Thin the paint with mineral spirits for a medium consistency so that it will not drip or '''lump'''.

